	As observed above, $i$ is a comorphism of sites $({\cal D}, M^{i}_{J})\to ({\cal C}, J\vee R_{i})$. On the other hand, by our hypothesis, $i$ is also a morphism of sites $({\cal D}, M^{i}_{J})\to ({\cal C}, J\vee R_{i})$ and hence it is $(K, J\vee R_{i})$-continuous. We can therefore apply Proposition \ref{proprecoverytopologycontinuity} to it. But, since $a_{J\vee R_{i}}\circ \textup{Lan}_{i^{\textup{op}}}$ preserves finite limits and hence monomorphisms, $\textup{Lan}_{i^{\textup{op}}}(m_{T})$ is $(J\vee R_{i})$-bicovering if and only if the flat functor $a_{J}\circ \textup{Lan}_{i^{\textup{op}}}\circ y_{\cal D}=l_{\cal C}\circ i$ sends $T$ to an epimorphic family of $\Sh({\cal C}, J\vee R_{i})$, that is, if and only if $i$ sends $T$ to a $(J\vee R_{i})$-covering family. 
