	(ii) $\imp$ (i) Since the construction of the geometric morphism induced by a comorphism of sites is functorial, and any canonical geometric inclusion $\Sh({\cal A}, Z) \hookrightarrow [{\cal A}^{\textup{op}}, \Set]$ is induced by the identity functor on $A$, regarded as comorphism of sites $({\cal A}, Z)\to ({\cal A}, T)$ where $T$ is the trivial topology on $\cal A$, we have a commutative square
	$$
	\xymatrix{
