\begin{proofs}
	Since $p$ is a discrete fibration, every arrow of $\cal D$ is cartesian and hence, by Proposition \ref{propliftcontinuity}, if $F\circ p$ is continuous then $F$ trivially satisfies the hypotheses of Proposition \ref{propcharcanonicalfunctors} with respect to every ($J$-covering) sieve on $\cal C$, that is, $F$ is continuous. Conversely, if $F$ is continuous then $F\circ p$ also is, since $p$ is continuous being a fibration.  
